{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37245-werewolf-the-apocalypse-reference-spreadsheet","id":37245,"title":"Werewolf: the Apocalypse Reference Spreadsheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T02:12:31-08:00","id":37245,"title":"Werewolf: the Apocalypse Reference Spreadsheet","content":"Hi everyone. This is my reference Excel spreadsheet for humans, Garou and Fera from the classic World of Darkness. I like to think of it as fairly complete, but would love any feedback you have. A couple things I intentionally left out were Wetware from <i>Demon Hunter X</i> and demonic investitures, because I don\u2019t really feel like they fit in with the Werewolf game. There are also some things in the database which I don\u2019t use in my own games (like the Gypsy stuff) but I included them for completion\u2019s sake. If you know of any content or book with something I\u2019ve missed, I\u2019d love to know about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/...Reference.xlsx</a><br /> <br /> I've cleaned up my thread here and will just make edits to this post in the future. Since my original post, I've updated this spreadsheet with information from pre-Modern Nights books of other lines, and some smattering of crossover-worthy details from Mage, as well as:<ul><li><i>Rage Across the World</i></li> <li><i>Dark Ages Darkening Sky</i></li> <li><i>Wyld West Expansion Pack</i></li> <li><i>Tribebook: White Howlers</i></li> <li><i>Book of the Wyrm - 20th Anniversary Edition</i></li> <li><i>W20: Umbra: The Velvet Shadow</i></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-Al