e-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T18:49:23-08:00","id":42091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37245-werewolf-the-apocalypse-reference-spreadsheet?p=41630#post41630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this resource, should make it a little easier to navigate my shelf of books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the exact reason I started the spreadsheet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T14:57:41-07:00","id":580268,"title":"","content":"In the document the Gift &quot;Silence&quot; is mentioned as Silent Strider Cliath and Ragabash Adren - although both are different gifts, that share a name and a kind of similar power, there are huge differences between them that would require them to be separate entries.<br /> <br /> Silent Strider Cliath from Werwolf revised:<br /> Like Blur of the Milkey Eye for sound. Increases any listeners difficulties by one per success. No cost. But roll.<br /> <br /> Ragabash Adren from 1st Edition Player's Guide:<br /> Pay two Gnosis to create a area (5 yard per success radius on dif 8 Manipulation + stealth roll) in which nobody/nothing can hear sound. Gifts that require sound (like Clap of Thunder) must win at a contested gnosis roll against the ragabash to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T00:12:54-07:00","id":592384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/37245-werewolf-the-apocalypse-reference-spreadsheet?p=580268#post580268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the document the Gift &quot;Silence&quot; is mentioned as Silent Strider Cliath and Ragabash Adren - although both are different gifts, that share a name and a kind of similar power, there are huge differences between them that would require them to be separate entries.<br /> <br /> Silent Strider Cliath from Werwolf revised:<br /> Like Blur of the Milkey Eye for sound. Increases any listeners difficulties by one per success. No cost. But roll.<br /> <br /> Ragabash Adren from 1st Edition Player's Guide:<br /> Pay two Gnosis to create a area (5 yard per success radius on dif 8 Manipulation + stealth roll) in which nobody/nothing can hear sound. Gifts that require sound (like Clap of Thunder) must win at a contested gnosis roll against the ragabash to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, man. It looks like the Ragabash Gift actually is the same as a Kitsune gift and I had listed it as Silence [Kitsune]. I will make that change and it will be fixed in the next update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<spa